WEBVTT

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.510
<i>Good morning, everyone.</i>

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:08.820
<i>Today the first-years will be competing 
in an orienteering activity as clubs.</i>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.400
<i>Your destinations are written 
on lots inside this box.</i>

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.510
<i>Once you arrive at your 
destination as a team,</i>

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.640
<i>get your cards stamped,
then draw your next destination.</i>

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.910
<i>You'll need a total of seven stamps.</i>

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.630
<i>You can't receive your stamps unless your 
entire group is present, so be careful.</i>

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:31.330
<i>Also, use of cell phones will not be allowed.</i>

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.010
<i>We'll be distributing cases.</i>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.640
<i>Once you put your phone inside, 
seal the case with a sticker.</i>

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.100
<i>If you use your phone outside of an 
emergency situation, you'll be disqualified.</i>

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.370
<i>Also, you may use trains, 
buses, and bicycles.</i>

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:48.480
<i>If you return to school by 5 PM with your
 entire group, you'll have completed the activity.</i>

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:52.620
<i>Could a representative from each 
team come draw a destination?</i>

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.330
Be careful and have fun.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.490
Okay.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.420
It's inconvenient that 
we can't use our phones.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.520
Lately, most phones have GPS built in.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.710
Where are we going first?

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:13.170
<b>Tsurugaoka Hachimangu</b>

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.170
We're starting at the Tsurugaoka Hachimangu shrine.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.000
Orienteering around Kamakura, huh?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.050
I'm excited.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.350
We're off!

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.340
Bear!

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.540
This is Tsurugaoka Hachimangu, huh?

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.570
It's huge.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:13.210
<b>#9  A Challenge From Mr. Bear!?</b>

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.080
If all we have to do is visit each 
destination and collect stamps,

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.210
this should be easy.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.770
So, where do we get our stamp?

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.850
Over there.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.330
What a great view!

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.560
Guys, hurry up!

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.220
She climbed those stairs quick.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.560
Apparently, Nagasaki has a lot of hills.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.650
We need to build up our stamina, 
or we'll get left behind.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.530
You're almost done!

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.860
You can do it!

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.820
Fuyune-san, you can do it!

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.650
I'm finally here.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.500
Stamp us, please.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.920
Okay, everyone's here. Good work.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.700
Where are we going next?

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:01.130
What?

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.590
<b>Zeniarai Benzaiten</b>

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.590
Z-Zeni... sen... ben?

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.900
It's the Zeniarai Benzaiten shrine.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.400
If the teams in this orienteering 
activity are broken up by club,

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.340
does that make this an 
extension of club activities?

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.550
Apparently.

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.610
Does that mean reaching the finish 
line counts as a club achievement?

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.050
Maybe.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.610
Then we'd better work hard.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.880
Let's follow President Akizuki's 
lead and do our best.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:29.830
Yeah.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.290
Are you sure you want me 
to be the club president?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.090
Of course.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.040
You're responsible.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:43.300
Yeah. You acted as our leader 
during the criterium, too.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.760
Be our president.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:46.960
Girls...

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.570
I don't have the confidence yet,

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.980
but I'll do my best as president 
of the bicycle club.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.600
The hills just keep going.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.900
My legs are starting to hurt.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.490
Are you okay?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.910
Tomo-chan, how much farther?

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.140
That gate is the entrance.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:13.870
We're almost there. You can do it, everyone.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.340
I can't believe there's another 
hill after the stone steps.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.400
<b>Zeniarai Benzaiten
Ugafuku Shrine</b>

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.800
The shrine is up this way.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:26.520
We're exploring.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.290
Or are we adventuring?

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.850
It's amazing that there's a shrine down here.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:35.310
<b>Zeniarai Benzaiten</b>

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:36.840
I wonder what Zeniarau Benzaiten means.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:43.320
If you wash your money in the spring at 
this convenient shrine, it multiplies.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.660
What? That's amazing!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.500
Let's go wash our money!

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.280
After we pay our respects.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.420
This is where you wash your money.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.520
What do we do with this?

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.700
First, put your money in the basket.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.640
Then pour water over it
using the ladle and wash it.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:15.270
Once you drain the water, you're finished.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:17.830
It's so simple.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.870
You don't need to pour 
that much water over it.

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.360
More water doesn't mean more money.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.390
I was just thinking it'd be nice
 if we became a proper club soon

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.490
and started receiving a budget.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.450
You're doing it for the bicycle club, huh?

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:41.080
Why don't we all do it again while 
praying for the bicycle club to be

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.060
officially recognized and receive a budget?

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:44.970
Yeah.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:53.680
<b>Genjiyama Yoritomozo</b>

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.650
Our next destination is Genjiyama.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.680
That's right next door.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.060
But there are more hills.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.200
What kind of orienteering activity is this?

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.250
We've been climbing all day.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.600
You can do it.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.240
Shall we take a break?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.490
Yeah.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.260
What's wrong?

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.500
I heard a sound.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.160
Is it a squirrel?

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.470
Maybe it was a monkey running away.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:27.840
It sounded bigger than that.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.210
Bear!

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:32.130
It's a bear!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:32.130
Bear!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:35.010
Bear, bear, bear, bear!

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:35.970
Huh?

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.180
Bear!

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.770
Bear, bear, bear, bear...

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.390
<b>Challenge</b>

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.390
Bear!

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:43.810
Bear!

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:44.850
What?

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.940
It's happening again!

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.500
Are you sure we should let them go?

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:55.350
They were in the night 
criterium, too, weren't they?

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.230
I wonder why they challenged us again.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:02.040
"I can't forget the humiliation 
I suffered at the criterium."

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.000
"I challenge you to a race 
so I can have my revenge."

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.420
"A one-on-one bike race against Maiharu."

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.130
Bear, bear, bear!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.090
I'm not making any progress.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:22.980
Bear... Bear, bear, bear, bear, bear!

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.400
Bear!

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.270
Wait.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.520
Bear!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:32.400
Bear, bear, bear!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.240
Should I be doing this?

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:43.890
I was biking around Kamakura 
and enjoying the sights, too.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:50.880
Mr. Bear, at this rate, we won't get to see 
the view on the other side of the pass.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.090
Don't you want to see it?

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.220
Jeez. In that case...

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.640
Bear, bear, bear, bear...

00:08:59.010 --> 00:08:59.640
Bear?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.100
Now, it's not a race.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:07.650
Mr. Bear, let's quit racing and 
enjoy the scenery together.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:08.900
Bear?

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.650
What a nice view.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.620
Look, you can even see the ocean.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:19.860
See?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:25.130
You'd rather pursue aesthetics 
over competition?

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.500
What an interesting girl.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.130
I don't need this.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:30.720
What?

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.070
Blonde hair?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.210
I'm Sandy McDougal.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.530
Nice to meet you.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:48.980
What?

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.320
Mr. Bear is a foreign student?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.120
Does that mean you're in Class E?

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.050
Yeah.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.110
But why did you want to challenge us again?

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.100
Because I'll keep challenging 
you until I win.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:03.400
Today, I have the same kind of bicycle you do.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.750
I wanted a fair challenge.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.270
I see.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:11.000
But today I lost to your passion, Hiromi.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.230
Riding bicycles and enjoying the scenery...

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:16.470
You have a truly wonderful heart.

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:20.450
I'd like to start enjoying cycling, too.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.680
Let's enjoy cycling together.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:27.500
What? But is it okay for you to come with us?

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.780
I thought you were part of the cosplay club.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:34.100
No, no. I haven't joined any club yet.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:37.760
I was only representing the 
cosplay club at the criterium.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.260
Really?

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:42.370
So please.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.030
Okay, let's ride around together.

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:46.760
Everyone's okay with that, right?

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:47.910
Why not?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:51.710
Yeah, but we'd better check with a teacher.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.860
Yes, got it.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:11:00.250
Sandy McDougal-san has been accepted as 
a provisional member of the bicycle club

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:03.890
and been allowed to change 
orienteering teams.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.600
They made an exception for you.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.200
All right. Thank you.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.200
Now, we can go together.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.310
Yeah. I'm so happy.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.150
<b>Kamakura
Buddha</b>

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:18.900
Shall we head to the next point?

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:26.450
Since it's all downhill to the 
giant Buddha, this is easy.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.290
Let's hurry, everyone.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.500
Yahoo!

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:36.530
Sandy, we ride on the left in Japan!

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.670
Oh, right.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:43.410
Awesome! The Buddha is very big!

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:47.140
Everyone, we should take 
a commemorative photo.

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.770
We get our stamp inside.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.780
What? Inside?

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:07.540
Amazing.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.260
Fantastic.

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.690
I can't believe it's empty.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:14.040
How did they make this Buddha?

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:18.630
Are those bumps on the 
roof the Buddha's head?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.160
Oh, interesting.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.930
That's what it looks like on the inside.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.090
How interesting.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.720
<b>Kamakura
Museum of
 Literature</b>

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.000
We just need one more.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.630
Choose your last destination.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:57.460
Good luck.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:58.920
Where's the last place?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.710
<b>Enoshima Tower</b>

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.170
What?

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:13.140
I can't believe we have to climb 
up there for our last stamp.

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:15.520
It's the last one. You can do it.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:20.230
I know, but my legs are exhausted 
from all the stone steps and hills.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:27.570
Tomo-chan, why don't we take a break?

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:30.410
I guess we can. There's still time.

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:35.030
The beach!

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.030
Wow, there's a bunch of something here.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:48.680
You're right.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:52.320
Is this seaweed?

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:55.510
Wow, it's very slimy.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:58.350
Hey, girls. Skipping class?

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:01.180
Manager! Tsuru-san!

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:03.190
A horse?

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.420
Hear, hear.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:09.890
I am Cycle Flat Manager, Hooji Korone.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.070
Hello.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:12.730
What a coincidence.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:16.070
And where did you get that horse?

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.750
It's Tsuru-chan's horse.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.720
The store's closed today, 
so we're out for a walk.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:25.260
My family runs a horse trekking business.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.760
What are you girls doing?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.180
We're orienteering today.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:33.180
We're exploring the city 
of Kamakura on our bikes.

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:36.370
Ah, that annual tradition.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.440
Huh? I don't recognize one of you.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.360
This is Mr. Bear.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.060
Hi.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.150
The fast one from the other day.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:48.200
He has such a kind face.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.920
I'd like to try riding him.

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:51.200
You want to ride him?

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.220
Can I?

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:56.410
Hiromi, would you like to ride together?

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:01.630
To thank you for the scenery you showed 
me today, I'd like to show you something.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.830
What?

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:09.000
We're so high up.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.260
The view from on top of a horse is nice, too.

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.680
Hiromi, look.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.680
Wow, it's Mt. Fuji.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:21.890
It's very beautiful today.

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:25.160
Hiromi, hold on tight.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:25.730
What?

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:26.980
Let's go.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:32.800
It's so fast.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.760
You really are a good rider.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:39.200
In my home state of Colorado, 
we ride horses instead of cars.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.210
Colorado?

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:44.280
Yes. It's a state in my country of America.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:47.020
There aren't any beaches,
but we have the Rocky Mountains.

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:49.170
It's a very beautiful place.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.300
They're full of energy.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.300
Yeah.

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:02.980
I'm exhausted after just a 
little extended climbing.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:07.190
I'm not sure if I'll be able to 
keep up with the rest of the club.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.140
It's okay.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.780
Besides, aren't you going 
to take lots of pictures?

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:14.450
How do you know about that?

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:18.750
I met your sister at the hospital.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.080
You're so nice, Fuyune-san.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:27.290
Fuyune-san...

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:32.550
I'll go with you, so let's go lots 
of places together in the future.

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:42.450
Sandy, why did you come to Japan?

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:45.940
I like Japanese anime and manga.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.560
I wanted to visit the 
country that produces them.

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:49.890
Really?

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:53.360
But weren't you scared to come 
to a foreign country by yourself?

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:54.780
Scared?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:58.320
We speak totally different 
languages, and the food...

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.290
No problem.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:03.230
I'd be going to the country 
I dreamed of visiting.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:06.960
When I made the decision to 
study abroad, I was overjoyed.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.820
Really?

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:12.080
Hiromi, is there anywhere you'd like to go?

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:16.880
I haven't thought about it yet.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:22.020
But I think riding bicycles is fun.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:25.950
Something always happens 
when I'm riding my bike.

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:29.250
I meet new people and make new friends.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:35.340
I met Tomo-chan, Fuyune-chan, Natsumi-chan,
and Shiki-sensei because of cycling.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:39.740
I even met you because of cycling.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.950
Oh, you're right.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:47.920
So right now, I think I'll ride my 
bike wherever my fancy takes me.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:51.960
How nice. I think that's a great idea.

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:56.370
Your bikes will rust if 
you don't wash them later.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.900
Be careful.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.560
We're back.

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:02.800
Sorry we're late.

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:06.010
How long were you going to make us wait?

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:09.520
Let's go get our last stamp.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.610
Are your legs okay?

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:15.570
Yeah. Thanks for letting me rest.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:18.570
Is everyone ready?

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.550
We're heading to the top 
of the Enoshima Tower.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.810
Let's head straight there.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:24.990
Yeah!

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.340
Fuyune-san, let's do it.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:28.610
Leave it to me.

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:29.650
Let's do it.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:30.630
Let's go.

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:53.220
Fuyune-san...

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:54.360
I'm okay.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.110
That's the finish line.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.820
We're almost there.

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:03.280
We're here!

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:08.000
Girls, over here.

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:09.960
Shiki-sensei.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.420
You're Sandy McDougal-san?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.010
Yes. I'm the bear.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:19.210
Oh, that was you?

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.090
Stamp, please.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.810
Congratulations. You completed your mission.

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:39.130
Now, we just have to head back to school.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.400
Yeah, about that.

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:44.180
Why don't you ride around 
together for a while longer?

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.660
You still have time.

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:48.250
What? Can we?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.950
As long as you're back by five.

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:52.120
Let's go, guys.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:52.870
Yeah!

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:55.370
Let's go cycling!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.450
But maybe we can eat first.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:39.860
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:43.180
<i>A-O-P: The first cycling club.</i>

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:55.870
<b>Shichirigahama</b>

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:55.870
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:55.870
<b>Enoshima Line</b>

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:55.870
<b>Kamakura Station</b>

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:55.870
<b>Yokosuka Line</b>

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:55.870
<b>Kamakura Cycling</b>

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:55.870
<b>Enoshima</b>

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:47.230
<i>Starting in this episode, 
we're finally going cycling.</i>

00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:49.500
<i>We'll start at Kamakura Station</i>

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:52.430
<i>and head towards Enoshima while 
enjoying the sights around town.</i>

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:54.040
<i>Our first destination is...</i>

00:21:55.760 --> 00:22:01.170
First, let's go see Kamakura's 
most handsome and hot man.

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:01.990
Handsome?

00:22:01.770 --> 00:22:05.720
<b>Kamakura's most handsome man!?</b>

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:05.160
<i>We're going to see Kamakura's 
most handsome man?!</i>

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:14.620
<b>Wakamiya Oji</b>

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:08.880
<i>It's time to start.</i>

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:12.720
<i>First, we'll head down Wakamiya 
Oji, a major thoroughfare.</i>

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:15.130
<i>Before long...</i>

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:17.140
I see something.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:18.980
Oh, wow.

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.430
It's the beach.

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:22.710
We're at the beach.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:27.340
<b>Yuigahama</b>

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:31.480
The sea breeze feels awesome.

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:32.200
* Filmed on bicycle and pedestrian path

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:41.080
<b>Kamakura Cycling</b>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:41.080
<b>Kamakura Station</b>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:41.080
<b>Yokosuka Line</b>

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:39.530
<i>The handsome man is over here, 
just off the coastal road.</i>

00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:43.610
<i>We're here.</i>

00:22:43.610 --> 00:22:48.420
<b>Kotokuin</b>

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:47.310
<i>Have you figured out who the handsome man is?</i>

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:51.710
I see. So that's what you meant by handsome man.

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:53.260
<b>Daiizan</b>

00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:52.050
Yeah. Have you figured it out?

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:52.720
Yeah.

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:54.530
And so...

00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:55.210
Okay.

00:22:55.210 --> 00:22:58.560
We're here.

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:00.020
He's so cool.

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:08.860
<b>Kamakura Buddha</b>

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:01.780
<i>That's right.</i>

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:06.920
<i>The handsome man is one of Japan's three 
great Buddhas, the Kamakura Buddha.</i>

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:14.380
<i>His long nose and smiling mouth 
are what make him so handsome.</i>

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:17.580
<i>His eyes face downward,</i>

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:21.920
<i>so he'll make eye contact with 
visitors when they look up at him.</i>

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:23.070
He's looking at us?

00:23:23.070 --> 00:23:24.300
Yeah, he's looking this way.

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:25.170
Oh, my.

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:26.070
Looking at us, isn't he?

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:27.200
What a lady-killer.

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:31.300
Stop by if you get the chance.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time
"Let's Go On a Trip!"</b>
